{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aegis/1506755-the-techines","id":1506755,"title":"The Techines!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aegis"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-03-28T09:49:35-07:00","id":1506755,"title":"The Techines!","content":"In most tellings of Rhea and her children only Zeus is preserved from being devoured by Cronos. But in some tales, Poseidon is also smuggled out to raised elsewhere. The people Rhea trusted Zeus to were the Telchines. These were the pre-Hellenic gods of Rhodes.<br /> <br /> The surviving tales of the Telchines associate them with sorcery and smithcraft. The Telchines are often represented in art as merfolk generally of a strange type.<br /> <br /> Although the Telchines raised Poseidon and had been friends with the Olympians and Rhea, they later revolted against the gods. By the classical period they had a sinister reputation.<br /> <br /> It seems to me that the Telchines in Aegis could be stranded aliens. Hostile to other entities which may be manipulating the PCs. The Telchines might make interesting foes who are sometimes friendly, or at least capable of bargining. A third force in any campaign.<br /> <br /> Reactions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 05-30-2023, 07:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-28T10:26:32-07:00","id":1506761,"title":"","content":"wouldit be tacky if i created a groupg of them called the &quot